# Damayan App — Role-Based System Overhaul

Restructure the entire app around **3 distinct user roles** with proper authentication flows, admin verification, coordinator tools, and donor/volunteer features.

---

## User Review Required

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **Role Consolidation**: You mentioned "Donor" and "Volunteer" as one combined role. The current app has them separate. I'm merging them into a single **"Donor/Volunteer"** role where users can both pledge supplies AND claim volunteer tasks. Please confirm this is correct.

> [!WARNING]
> **Breaking Change**: The current login system is a simple role-picker with no real authentication. This overhaul replaces it with a full Registration → Login → Verification flow. All existing "instant login" behavior will be removed.

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **No Backend**: Since there's no backend/database, all data (users, verification status, etc.) will be stored in Zustand state with `localStorage` persistence. This means data resets on cache clear. Is that acceptable for this phase, or should we add a lightweight backend (e.g., Firebase)?

